{"term":"rival","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a1b5665c92472c6d20","definition":"A competitor (person, team, company, etc.) with the same goal as another, or striving to attain the same thing. Defeating a rival may be a primary or necessary goal of a competitor.","example":"Chris is my biggest rival in the 400-metre race.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["archrival","arch-rival","corival","nonrival","rivaless","rivalise","rivalism","rivality","rivalization","rivalize","rivalless","rivalmance","rivalry","rivalship","rivalsome"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rival#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:501bd8879fccfeb64e","definition":"Someone or something with similar claims of quality or distinction as another.","example":"As a social historian, he has no rival.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["archrival","arch-rival","corival","nonrival","rivaless","rivalise","rivalism","rivality","rivalization","rivalize","rivalless","rivalmance","rivalry","rivalship","rivalsome"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rival#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c31cdbc4540ce00951","definition":"One having a common right or privilege with another; a partner.","example":"If you do meet Horatio and Marcellus, / The rivals of my watch, bid them make haste.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["archrival","arch-rival","corival","nonrival","rivaless","rivalise","rivalism","rivality","rivalization","rivalize","rivalless","rivalmance","rivalry","rivalship","rivalsome"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sour